<title>CANADA: ATHLETICS-RESULTS FROM THE ONE-ON-ONE CHALLENGE OF CHAMPIONS.</title>
<headline>ATHLETICS-RESULTS FROM THE ONE-ON-ONE CHALLENGE OF CHAMPIONS.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-06-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results from the One-On-One</p>
<p>Challenge of Champions athletics meet Sunday at the SkyDome:</p>
<p>Women's long jump</p>
<p> 1. Heike Drechsler (Germany)	  6.82 meters</p>
<p> 2. Jackie Joyner-Kersee (U.S.)	6.79</p>
<p>Men's high jump</p>
<p> 1. Charles Austin (U.S.)		2.30 meters</p>
<p> 2. Patrik Sjoberg (Sweden)	    2.20</p>
<p>:</p>
<p>Women's 100-meter hurdles</p>
<p> 1. Ludmila Engquist (Sweden)	 12.82 seconds</p>
<p> 2. Michelle Freeman (Jamaica)	12.96</p>
<p>Men's pole vault</p>
<p> 1. Okkert Brits (South Africa)	5.90 meters</p>
<p> 2. Lawrence Johnson (U.S.)	    5.75</p>
<p>Men's 150-meter sprint</p>
<p> 1. Donovan Bailey (Canada)	   14.99 seconds</p>
<p> 2. Michael Johnson (U.S.)	    did not finish</p>
